    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0374" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/7–1846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-18T15:00:00-04:00">July 18, 1946—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>671. President spoke on radio at noon saying Government was in full control and
                    blamed subversive movement on Rosca.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d300-f1"/> Sporadic
                    shooting continues and streets are so dangerous I have so far held <pb
                        facs="0375" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/> entire staff in building. Two municipal
                    armed policemen again invaded building and succeeded in reaching roof. I have
                    already protested this by telephone and intend to follow up with note.</p>
                <p>Three known killed, toll may be higher. There appears to be little coordination
                    among Government forces with Army again playing negative role. Armed (rifle)
                    pro-Government civilians have again appeared in streets. Not more than a dozen
                    students of 400 demonstrating have arms and they are pistols. Student riot also
                    unorganized.</p>
                <p>Send copies War Department and FBI.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d300-f1" n="34" xml:id="d300-f1-content">
                <p>Term applied to capitalist enterprises or vested interests.</p>
            </note>
